 {"id":"fabro-cc23","title":"Projectize prime boilerplate with the real gate in AGENTS.md","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-02T18:55:18.535Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-02T18:55:18.535Z","description":"In run 01M0QTNF6GWHGPKHSQ2Y2PB8CQ, planner@1 and implementer@1 each ran sd prime/ml prime and ingested ~5 KB of generic template including a close-protocol demanding bun test && bun run lint && bun run typecheck — commands that do not exist in this Go repo, whose gate is just qualitygate. Add a project-override note in AGENTS.md outside the tool-generated seeds-onboard markers: this repo's close protocol is just qualitygate, and bun-based prime instructions do not apply. Expected effect: removes wrong-stack misexecution risk and stops contradictory context in every agent stage."}
 {"id":"fabro-3814","title":"Tell implementer to skip sd prime when the brief is already in context","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-02T18:55:18.711Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-02T18:55:18.711Z","description":"In run 01M0QTNF6GWHGPKHSQ2Y2PB8CQ, implementer@1 ran sd prime even though current_seed_brief already carried the seed context, adding ~5 KB to the costliest stage (implementer was /bin/bash.118 of the run's /bin/bash.181, 65%). Add one line to .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/implementer.md: skip sd prime when current_seed_brief is already in context. Expected effect: trims ~5 KB per implementer visit with no information loss."}
